WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
You've spoken a lot about empathy,

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:09.730
and it's impossible for me not to mention.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.370
We've actually had almost
two weeks of shows,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.890
I believe now, where
we've not once mentioned

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.110
the president of the United States

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.310
because I haven't wanted him to be a part

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.770
of the conversation.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.740
I've wanted the conversation
to go deeper than that.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.410
But I'll bring him up now
because we have a leader

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:32.150
of the country who I
think everyone would agree

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.703
has a chronic inability
to demonstrate empathy.

00:00:37.998 --> 00:00:41.500
I feel that that has been a,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.700
a situation like what
happened after the killing

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.470
of George Floyd is, as crazy as it sounds,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.390
it's an opportunity for change.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.620
It's an opportunity for the
president of the United States

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.120
to bring us all together
and to say beautiful things

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.510
that might actually bring
about lasting change.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:01.990
And I feel that that has been
squandered by our president.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.170
Yeah, so I love you for not centering him

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.940
in your conversations
'cause it's not about him.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.970
This election coming up is
not a referendum on one guy

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.803
and one office.

00:01:11.803 --> 00:01:13.340
It's really referendum on who we are

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.200
and who we're gonna be to each other.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.380
And we've got to raise the
frequency in our nation

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.620
in terms of the love and empathy.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.820
But you mentioned him,
so let me just say this.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.400
I just fundamentally believe,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.120
and I've watched leaders
on both sides of the aisle

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.110
demonstrate this.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.760
You can't lead the people if
you don't love the people.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.380
And he just does not love all Americans.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.840
You don't have to agree
with all Americans.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.170
But his willingness to so cavalierly deny

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.850
so many Americans human dignity,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:49.850
for him to trample upon the very humanity

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.010
of other Americans to cheapen this nation

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.790
by working so hard to divide us

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.430
and to make us hate each other.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.930
All of those things
mean he is illegitimate

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.160
in the kind of moral
leadership that we need.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.510
He may have the trappings of power.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.620
He may have the title of the office,

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.640
but the title doesn't make the man,

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:10.700
the man has to make the title.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.830
And he has been a failure,

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:16.070
a failure in a moral
office that Republicans

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:21.070
from Lincoln to Democrats like Obama

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.870
who have led with love for their country,

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.120
with malice towards none,
with charity towards all.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.060
He's had so much malice towards so many

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.840
and so little charity towards others.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.680
So I just want this to be
a moral moment in America.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.270
And I'm so proud of his
former cabinet members

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.570
and national Republicans
who are coming forward

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:43.780
and saying just that.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.020
That this man is uniquely unqualified

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.220
for this moment in history.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.770
And he has cheapened, to
me, the greatest ideal

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:52.750
in all of humanity,

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:56.270
which America has driven
in every generation

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.950
to make manifest in this world,

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.950
is that we are a nation of
love where we love one another.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.080
He is so failed to be in the fight

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.660
to make us a more loving nation,

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.010
or as King would say, a
more beloved community.

00:03:09.424 --> 00:03:13.823
I have so much hurt for
what he's done to people.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.630
And I've watched it.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.420
I've watched people.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.520
We call some countries shithole countries.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.630
I've seen people, immigrants come to me,

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.270
begging me to do something about it.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.093
I've watched him degrade.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.930
You know, I talked to a
college friend of mine

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.027
whose kid was in Lafayette
Park when he stormed in,

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.600
had people storm in with
rubber bullets and tear gas.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.150
And the anguish that somebody would think

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.100
in this sacred Capitol where people

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.250
from the March on Washington
to Second Amendment

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.160
rights people have come for generations

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.060
to peacefully petition their government.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.900
And he just tramples that for what?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.190
A national security issue

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.740
because he had to urgently get someone?

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.500
Nope, to hold up a book
that he should read

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.443
that talks about humility and the meek.

00:04:07.771 --> 00:04:09.300
I can't give him more of my energy.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.160
I wanna give it to us.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.150
I wanna give it to love.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.810
I wanna give it to good
people who right now

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.160
don't understand the
urgency for them to act.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.410
That's where I wanna give it.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:21.010
He's not the center of my concern,

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:24.000
and I appreciate you having
a show that reflects that.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.380
Well, you know, I have not wanted to

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.370
do Trump jokes or make
it all about Donald Trump

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.673
because ultimately, I find
him very uninteresting

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.310
and his actions sadden me.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:45.220
But I'm angry.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.030
I reserved my anger for
people that enable him.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.950
That's what makes me angry.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:53.573
And I get very angry at
people who do know better,

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:59.734
who are in a party that may be
in the short term benefiting

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.840
from the fact that he holds that office.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.200
But in the long-term, I
don't know how they're gonna

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.610
be able to talk to their
kids or their grandchildren.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.740
And so I've been very moved by,

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:12.500
especially the military
leadership that's come forward.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.230
Mattis, Kelly, most recently Colin Powell,

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.680
that is something that
the Republican party

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.680
does show respect for, is
our military leadership.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.960
And when you have these
prominent members of the military

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.440
speaking out, my heart swells with pride.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.670
I'm very happy that
people are coming forward.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.040
I just wish there were more.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:38.580
I wish there were more
people who would step forward

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.937
and say, "You know what?

00:05:39.937 --> 00:05:42.757
"Yes, we got some good court appointments.

00:05:42.757 --> 00:05:45.427
"Yes, we got some stuff done

00:05:45.427 --> 00:05:48.607
"because we had someone in the Oval office

00:05:48.607 --> 00:05:52.510
"who would do our bidding,
but this is too much."

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.430
I wish we'd hear from more
politicians like that.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.723
Well, we've heard throughout
history the bystander.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.410
King talked about we have to
repent in our day and age,

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.920
not simply for the vitriolic
words and violent actions

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.570
of the bad people, but the silence

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.680
and inaction of the good people.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.660
I think that you're right.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:11.800
And I think that this, again,

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.860
is that moment in American history.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.240
And I actually feel sorry
for the Republican party

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.981
because as a lot of his
primary opponents in 2016,

00:06:19.981 --> 00:06:22.120
'15 and '16 said, they predicted.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.550
Lindsey Graham, all of them predicted

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.260
that he would destroy
the Republican party.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.850
And a lot of them have gone silent now

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:30.410
and are refusing to tell
the truth of the perversion,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.500
the meanness, that he's
cavalier, and the meanness

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.580
that isn't at the heart
of a lot of Republicans.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.650
You named some of them like Colin Powell.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:42.300
And so this is ultimately a
test, and a test isn't over.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.310
This is a president who could disrespect

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:47.750
the peaceful transition of
power in 150 days if you lose.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.310
He's already trying to
de-legitimize the election.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.900
This is a president that's capable,

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.900
has shown us that he's
capable of anything.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:57.677
And so the stress test on
this nation over the next 150,

00:06:57.677 --> 00:06:59.283
160 days are gonna be great.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:03.700
And this is a defining
moment for all of us.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.993
And in a defining moment,

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.570
you're not defined by what happens to you.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.190
This guy's capable of anything.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.993
You're always defined by
how you choose to respond.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:15.773
I agree with you.

00:07:15.773 --> 00:07:18.340
I'm happy for those who
have decided to respond

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.310
by not silence, but by speaking up,

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:22.833
by lifting their voices
to be heard by history.

